<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss May car registrations fall 9.4 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Swiss May car registrations fall 9.4 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>New car registrations in Switzerland and Liechtenstein fell 9.4 percent in May from a year earlier to 27,283 vehicles.</p>
<p>There was a cumulative 4.4 percent decline to 95,712 in the first four months of the year, the Swiss Automobile Importers Association said.</p>
<p>Leading exporters:</p>
<p>					May 1997	 May 1996</p>
<p>    Germany			 11,899	   13,430</p>
<p>    France			   4,098	   4,307</p>
<p>    Italy			    1,863	   2,448</p>
<p>    Japan			    6,424	   6,613</p>
<p>    Sweden			   800	     826</p>
<p>    Britain			  426	     391</p>
<p>    Korea			    514	     427</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom +41-1-631 7340</p>
</text>
